  "text": "I added memoization to `fib` in `fib.js`. It keeps each answer in a `Map` at the top of the file, so each value of `n` is only calculated once and later calls reuse it.\n\n**Test results:**\n- `fib(10) === 55` and `fib(50) === 12586269025` both came back correct.\n- `node fib.js 1000` now finishes in 0.03 seconds. With the old code, my first test run didn't finish within the 120-second limit.\n\n**Two limits remain:**\n- **Very large n crashes:** `node fib.js 20000` failed with an error. It's most likely a stack overflow, because the function still calls itself thousands of levels deep. Rewriting `fib` as a simple loop would fix this and wouldn't need the cache at all. Say if you want me to switch to that.\n- **Answers past n = 78 aren't exact:** JavaScript numbers lose precision there. For example, `fib(90)` printed 2880067194370816000, which isn't the true value. If you need exact results, the fix is to use `BigInt`."
 },
